stable-diffusion.cpp provides diffusion model (SD, Flux, Wan, Qwen
Image, Z-Image, ...) inference in pure C/C++.

Features:
- Plain C/C++ implementation based on ggml, working in the same way as llama.cpp
- Super lightweight and without external dependencies
- Supports Image Models, Image Edit Models and  Video Models
- PhotoMaker support.
- IP-Adapter support (SD 1.5 and SDXL, including Plus)
- Control Net support with SD 1.5
- ADetailer
- LoRA support, same as stable-diffusion-webui
- Latent Consistency Models support (LCM/LCM-LoRA)
- Faster and memory efficient latent decoding with TAESD
- Upscale images generated with ESRGAN

If you have vulkan-sdk 1.4+, vulkan backend will be built, use VULKAN=no
to disable.

Optional dependencies (autodetected):
- cudatoolkit_13 - for CUDA backend, use CUDA=no to disable
- rocmtoolkit_7 - for HIP backend, use HIP=no to disable
- OpenBLAS - for BLAS backend, use OPENBLAS=no to disable
- nodejs - for WebUI
